This is quite similar to how I feel about it.

The starting pet and the not too rare tripe rations provide a quite easy
way to have both, items and protection. I happen to like stealing from
shops with a pet; the mechanics are intereseting, and quite obviously it
is meant as an alternative way to acquire valuable items without spending
money, or the apport property wouldn't exist. That said, sometimes,
eg when I don't have tripe or when I'm roleplaying a lawful character,
I'll just take the shortcut and buy all the really interesting stuff. It
really is better value for money than protection in the early game;
later on, when you want all the AC you can get, you'll have the money.

